{
    // PricedOrder var 2: the least principal a lender pays, from a simple block yield that moves in a
    // straight line between two points in time, so an order can rise or fall without updates.
    // R9 = (start height, start yield, end height, end yield), yields in bps per 262800 blocks, >= 0,
    //   and end height > start height. The yield is the start yield up to the start height, the end
    //   yield from the end height on, and on the straight line between them in between. Equal yields
    //   give one fixed rate. Clients put the end at or near the order's expiry.
    // With D = maturity - HEIGHT blocks left, L = end - start, at = HEIGHT clamped to [start, end],
    // and the yield taken exactly as Y / L, Y = y0 * L + (y1 - y0) * (at - start):
    //   principal * (B * L + Y * D) >= R * B * L, B = 10000 * 262800.
    // That is principal >= R / (1 + yield * D / B): the price at which the lender earns the yield.
    // The comparison is exact: no division and no rounding.
    // The shell additionally enforces the borrower's fixed principal floor and actual payment record.
    // Uses remaining blocks, not calendar time, market rates or compounding. Fees are not included:
    // a borrower quotes a little above a lend offer's yield to leave room for its batcher fee.
    // Fixed and on-close maturity only. A window order (mode 2) is refused: the shell would read this
    // payload's start height as the window's maximum duration. Window orders use CurveOrder_Pricing.
    val payload = SELF.R9[Coll[Long]].get
    if (payload.size != 4 || SELF.R4[Coll[Long]].get(6) == 2L) {
        sigmaProp(false)
    } else {
        val bond = OUTPUTS(1)
        val borrower = bond.R6[Coll[Long]].get
        val remaining = bond.R9[Coll[Long]].get(2) - HEIGHT.toLong
        val principal = if (CONST_REPAYMENT_TOKEN == SELF.id.slice(0, 0)) borrower(1)
            else bond.R7[Coll[(Coll[Byte], Long)]].get(0)._2
        val start = payload(0)
        val startYield = payload(1)
        val end = payload(2)
        val endYield = payload(3)
        val now = HEIGHT.toLong
        val at = if (now < start) start else if (now > end) end else now
        val span = (end - start).toBigInt
        val rate = startYield.toBigInt * span + (endYield.toBigInt - startYield.toBigInt) * (at - start).toBigInt
        val scale = 2628000000L.toBigInt
        sigmaProp(
            startYield >= 0L && endYield >= 0L && end > start &&
            remaining > 0L && principal > 0L && borrower(0) > 0L &&
            principal.toBigInt * (scale * span + rate * remaining.toBigInt) >=
                borrower(0).toBigInt * scale * span)
    }
}
